course: dictionary
lesson: 5582
title: A helper in the Temple
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A Levite was a man from the tribe of Levi. The Levites served in the Temple, helping the priests, singing and caring for holy things. Think of them as helpers who worked in a holy place.
explain: In Jesus's story «a priest and a Levite passed by on the other side of the road.» Both were religious helpers, yet both walked past a hurt man. The clue is in the word passed: they did not stop to help.
explain: Jesus told this parable, a story that teaches a lesson, to answer the question «Who is my neighbour?» The lesson is that being religious is not enough; you must also show love to your neighbour. The Samaritan stopped and helped, and that is the example to follow.
fact: A Levite was a man from the tribe of Levi who helped in the Temple.
fact: Levites helped the priests, sang and cared for holy things.
fact: In old Bible stories, Levites carried the Ark of the Covenant.
fact: In the Good Samaritan, «a priest and a Levite passed by on the other side of the road».
fact: Being religious is not enough; you must also show love to your neighbour.
exercise: «A priest and a Levite passed by on the other side of the road.» What did the Levite do to the hurt man? | Stopped and bandaged his wounds | Paid for his care | Carried him to the Temple | *Walked past without helping
exercise: What was the job of a Levite in the Temple? | Ruling the country | *Helping the priests, singing and caring for holy things | Building walls around the city | Selling goods to the visitors
exercise: In the Good Samaritan story, what is the lesson? | *Being religious is not enough; you must also show love to your neighbour | Only priests can help people who are hurt | Lawyers always tell the truth | Robbers should be left alone
test: Which tribe did a Levite come from? | The tribe of Benjamin | The tribe of Dan | The tribe of Judah | *The tribe of Levi
test: Who did the Levites help in the Temple? | The listeners | The robbers | The Samaritans | *The priests
exam: In Jesus's story, what did the priest and the Levite have in common? | *Both passed by the hurt man without helping | Both were Samaritans who paid for his care | Both bandaged the hurt man's wounds | Both were robbers who had hurt him
